{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549222-m20-what-level-of-correspondence-to-allow-other-creature-use-their-powers-remotely","id":1549222,"title":"[M20] What level of Correspondence to allow other creature use their powers remotely?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-12T18:41:04-07:00","id":1549222,"title":"[M20] What level of Correspondence to allow other creature use their powers remotely?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As per the title thread. Essentially, I was reading some effects you use at a rating on yourself, a higher rating on someone else (Mind's mental shield effect is 1 dot for you, but 2 dots to apply to someone else). So, what level of Correspondence (and any other relevant sphere) to let another creature, whether a Mage or any super, use their powers remotely?<br /> <br /> IF feasible, it seems that Correspondence would have to be at least the one level higher than the desired sphere, since you have to use the same level of Correspondence than the Sphere that you plan to use remotely yourself, so one level higher for another character seems reasonable. But if I want to let my Garou friend use their <i>Sense Wyrm</i>, or<i> Scent of the True Form</i> on a remote location, then what do I use?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-22-2025, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T05:26:39-07:00","id":1549229,"title":"","content":"I think this goes in sending senses category and that would be Cor 2. So for someone else given that logic it would be 3.<br /> I can however see a ST that would say you have to recreate the whole power with awakened magic and lock it on the friend in order for it to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T12:37:09-07:00","id":1549253,"title":"","content":"Depends on the level of remote viewing desired? The +1 Rank is probably a decent way to handle using Landscape of the Mind (Corr 1 on yourself) or Sense Through Space (Corr 2) on other creatures for them to be able to use their own powers. When we get into Correspondence 3+ effects it feels like it should move to higher successes required and potentially additional Spheres to ensure that supernatural senses can make use of the manipulations of spatial relations. When you're at the point of being able to open magical gateways where anyone can just walk through a doorway/etc. and end up somewhere completely different, the idea of needing even higher level magic to let someone smell something on the other side of it feels a rather off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T13:02:59-07:00","id":1549254,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> thanks for your opinions.<br /> <br /> I started with sensory powers because those are the ones that are mainly relevant to the situation we have at the table, but yes, after having colocation and portals the question becomes moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T13:33:55-07:00","id":1549258,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I wasn't a bit more clear. What I said largely applies beyond projecting sensory powers further. It would also apply to supernatural powers that have sensory conditions to meet.<br /> <br /> For example if a power can only be used on a target you can see, your Mage buddy with Correspondence could let you see around corners and direct your power without being in the line-of-sight of the target. What the power actually doesn't really wouldn't change that (at least not at a baseline metaphysical level for Mage, crossover can get wildly out of hand with such combos and past books have suggested upping Sphere requirements as a matter of game balance). The Garou Gift list includes a power that lets them use howls to deal damage to any target that can hear them, and they can see clearly (it's a higher level power for obvious reasons there). The Garou have plenty of powers to extend their visual range, but not so many for seeing around buildings. Saying it's Correspondence 2 to grant a werewolf visual &quot;lock on&quot; around corners or whatnot is a valid reading of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}